{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he who did not, etc. — and he left.</b> The reason the verse says <b>וַיַּעֲזֹב</b> with the added vav is that the full measure of the verse is as follows: he who did not set his heart to any of the preceding words of HaShem — he added to his sin even in a matter such as this, in which he suffers no loss by bringing them indoors, and he stands to lose his possessions; nevertheless, <b>וַיַּעֲזֹב</b> etc., to show that he despised the word of HaShem. And it occurred to me that the Egyptians were provokers of the Place — not because they clung to Israel for their servitude is the reason they refused to send them off; rather, behold, it is evident before you that they did not believe that there was any power in Him, heaven forfend, to bring down the hail, and even by way of doubt they did not have it in them, for they were not concerned to protect their servants and their livestock. Or perhaps it is because since in the six preceding plagues there was no such wondrous thing, they did not take from them the measure that He is able to do it, and it seemed in their eyes far-fetched that He could do it."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "Reading המקום as the divine epithet 'the Place'; reading לצד... הוא שהיו as 'not because... is the reason that...'; the clause כי יכול לה may be elliptical for כי יכול לעשותו, rendered 'that He is able to do it.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:12.622760997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}